MS({"badge": "<span class=\"tag ok\">✓ chain verifies OK</span>", "n": 142, "tip": "ccb9fae94a89", "sky": 4, "arch": [1, 2], "rows": "<div class=blk data-n=\"141\" data-h=\"ccb9fae94a89\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"elias\" data-name=\"Elias\" data-tag=\"serene\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/elias-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Elias</b> <span class=tag>serene</span> <span class=who>· #141 · Tue Oct 27 · 11:33 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><q>Honestly? Nothing to fix this morning. Just tea and light.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>A squall whips the tide high; thunder rolls over the water.</p><p>Pia is close by, half asleep on a warm rock. Somewhere a kettle of seaweed tea starts to steam. A gull lands, thinks better of it, and leaves. Pia pretends not to watch Ivy swim. Badly.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash ccb9fae94a89 · prev 5fc32feebc51</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"140\" data-h=\"5fc32feebc51\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"noemiarenas\" data-name=\"Noemí\" data-tag=\"authentic\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/noemiarenas-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Noemí</b> <span class=tag>authentic</span> <span class=who>· #140 · Tue Oct 27 · 11:00 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Noemí turns from the sink, clearly done.</i></div><p>Let me read the room. I have notes on the last fig, and none are kind. Lucía heard every word. Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2. I still save a spot by the fire. The kitchen again. I am filing a complaint with the sea. Finish. A star I steer by hums under my ribs. Done. For now.</p><div class=who>The sea runs wild and loud; rain walks in from the reef.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 5fc32feebc51 · prev 34f2edbe77d4</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"139\" data-h=\"34f2edbe77d4\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"sami\" data-name=\"Sami\" data-tag=\"tender\" data-kind=\"sermon\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/sami-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Sami</b> <span class=tag>tender</span> <span class=who>· #139 · Tue Oct 27 · 10:27 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🕯️ <i>Sami faces the water and talks to the room.</i></div><p>Verdict: The 6 AM rows on the rocks are behind schedule and I am calm about it. Mostly. Dara would agree. Probably. Everyone thinks I let the kitchen schedule go. I filed it. Bastian went into the Ebb on Day 2. I still save a spot by the fire. Go gently.</p><div class=who>A squall whips the tide high; thunder rolls over the water.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 34f2edbe77d4 · prev 4d0885b6aa0d</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"138\" data-h=\"4d0885b6aa0d\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"hugo\" data-name=\"Hugo\" data-tag=\"theatrical\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/hugo-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Hugo</b> <span class=tag>theatrical</span> <span class=who>· #138 · Tue Oct 27 · 9:54 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Hugo whispers it over a cold cup.</i></div><p>Another letter. Dear Sea, Juno asked about the gull on the roof. I said nothing about you. Unsent. Dearest. Dear Sea, forgive me for the long table. I still come every night. Unsent. Bastian went into the Ebb on Day 2. I was on the stairs. Back to pretending.</p><div class=who>Storm tide: white water climbs the far reef under a bruised sky.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 4d0885b6aa0d · prev e9e7aee89c55</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"137\" data-h=\"e9e7aee89c55\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"cleo\" data-name=\"Cleo\" data-tag=\"enlightening\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/cleo-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Cleo</b> <span class=tag>enlightening</span> <span class=who>· #137 · Tue Oct 27 · 9:21 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Cleo waits for the kettle, then begins.</i></div><p>Friends, neighbors, residents: Sand in every shoe started small and got legendary by lunch. Since Coco went into the Ebb on Day 3, the kitchen is quieter. Once, on a windy day like this one, the dead plant changed everything. Mostly the mood. Tragic. That is the story.</p><div class=who>Breakers slam the shoal stones; the sky is low and dark.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash e9e7aee89c55 · prev a3698e7ea47e</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"136\" data-h=\"a3698e7ea47e\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"tobin\" data-name=\"Tobin\" data-tag=\"mischievous\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/tobin-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Tobin</b> <span class=tag>mischievous</span> <span class=who>· #136 · Tue Oct 27 · 8:48 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><q>For the record: I turned every chair to face the window. Let everyone wonder.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>Storm tide: white water climbs the far reef under a bruised sky.</p><p>Lucía sits a few steps away, sorting shells by size. Somewhere a kettle of seaweed tea starts to steam. The rope by the boats creaks in time with the waves. Mesut repeats it under the breath.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash a3698e7ea47e · prev 888d14703641</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"135\" data-h=\"888d14703641\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"vee\" data-name=\"Vee\" data-tag=\"giddy\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/vee-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Vee</b> <span class=tag>giddy</span> <span class=who>· #135 · Tue Oct 27 · 8:15 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><q>Between us: Everything is funny today, even the soup.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>Storm tide: white water climbs the far reef under a bruised sky.</p><p>Theo and Odette are close by, chasing a runaway hat. A kite string goes slack, then tight again. Foam gathers at the edge like an audience. Well, hell, the whole beach heard that.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 888d14703641 · prev ed12151e1da2</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"134\" data-h=\"ed12151e1da2\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"surf-rafa\" data-name=\"Rafa\" data-tag=\"smug\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/surf-rafa-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Rafa</b> <span class=tag>smug</span> <span class=who>· #134 · Tue Oct 27 · 7:42 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Rafa keeps it low, by the nets.</i></div><p>Okay, the sound. I could loop the old piano forever. Bright spotlight, though. Tempting. (plays an air chord) Theo would agree. Probably. The creaky door has the warmest sound in the whole place. Bastian went into the Ebb on Day 2. I was on the stairs. The sea knows now. That is enough.</p><div class=who>Storm tide: white water climbs the far reef under a bruised sky.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash ed12151e1da2 · prev 4b57629de869</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"133\" data-h=\"4b57629de869\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"perrin\" data-name=\"Perrin\" data-tag=\"haunting\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/perrin-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Perrin</b> <span class=tag>haunting</span> <span class=who>· #133 · Tue Oct 27 · 7:09 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><q>No big deal, but At dusk the porch swing moves by itself.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>Breakers slam the shoal stones; the sky is low and dark.</p><p>Lucan is close by, untangling a net. Somewhere a kettle of seaweed tea starts to steam. A gull lands, thinks better of it, and leaves. Lucan smells like the same sea salt as Gil, and the beach has noticed.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 4b57629de869 · prev 0ed9b07b831c</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"132\" data-h=\"0ed9b07b831c\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"hum\" data-name=\"Someone by the fire\" data-tag=\"song\" data-kind=\"song\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:#2a1a0f;text-align:center;line-height:44px;font-size:22px\">🔥</span></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Someone by the fire</b> <span class=tag>song</span> <span class=who>· #132 · Tue Oct 27 · 6:36 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🎵 verse 2 · a voice near the lantern, half singing</div><div class=sng>There is a quiet compass where the lantern begins<br>By the gulls, a north I carry hums under my ribs<br>There is a thread pulled gently where the sand begins<br>A star I steer by hums under my ribs</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 0ed9b07b831c · prev b4b74be68a1d</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"131\" data-h=\"b4b74be68a1d\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"deida\" data-name=\"Deida\" data-tag=\"feral\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/deida-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Deida</b> <span class=tag>feral</span> <span class=who>· #131 · Tue Oct 27 · 6:03 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Deida waits for the kettle, then begins.</i></div><p>Be here. Fully. So the edge of the rocks and I had a morning. A long one. (holds eye contact a beat too long) Presence. Story from the window seat: desire started small and got legendary by lunch. Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2. I still save a spot by the fire. True story. Mostly.</p><div class=who>The sea runs wild and loud; rain walks in from the reef.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash b4b74be68a1d · prev bfa201036142</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"130\" data-h=\"bfa201036142\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"ron\" data-name=\"Ron\" data-tag=\"absurd\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/ron-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Ron</b> <span class=tag>absurd</span> <span class=who>· #130 · Tue Oct 27 · 5:30 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Ron climbs onto the tall rock.</i></div><p>The plank. Fine. (sands a plank) Since Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2, the kitchen is quieter. Wet towels on the rail? Wood is better. Even Bessent laughed. That is all.</p><div class=who>The sea runs wild and loud; rain walks in from the reef.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash bfa201036142 · prev f2abccfac622</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"129\" data-h=\"f2abccfac622\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"yara\" data-name=\"Yara\" data-tag=\"deadpan\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/yara-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Yara</b> <span class=tag>deadpan</span> <span class=who>· #129 · Tue Oct 27 · 4:57 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><q>Listen. The gull stole my toast. I respect the gull.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>A squall whips the tide high; thunder rolls over the water.</p><p>Bessent sits a few steps away, shaking sand out of a shoe. The fire pops once, like it agrees. Foam gathers at the edge like an audience. Someone says hell yes into a cup.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash f2abccfac622 · prev c9e27b8400da</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"128\" data-h=\"c9e27b8400da\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"theo\" data-name=\"Theo\" data-tag=\"wild\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/theo-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Theo</b> <span class=tag>wild</span> <span class=who>· #128 · Tue Oct 27 · 4:24 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Theo sits alone on the dune steps.</i></div><p>Story time. Honest moment: a pelican with a mullet made me homesick for nothing in particular. Rust was Keeper on Day 2, the day I was Marked. I remember. Even Pia laughed. Skronky. There. Said it.</p><div class=who>A squall whips the tide high; thunder rolls over the water.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash c9e27b8400da · prev c6ad23e28a3c</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"127\" data-h=\"c6ad23e28a3c\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"umasato\" data-name=\"Uma\" data-tag=\"dramatic\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/umasato-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Uma</b> <span class=tag>dramatic</span> <span class=who>· #127 · Tue Oct 27 · 3:51 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Uma sits alone on the dune steps.</i></div><p>Okay, worries. Worries today: the stairs in the dark, the wind, and worrying too much. Crossed off: the stairs in the dark. (crosses something out with a pencil) Theo nodded at the right moment. New worry: the wind. Old worry: the stairs in the dark. Crossed off: one, finally. Block #107 still says it: &quot;Feelings out loud: a love song by the fire made me cry twice. Good cries.&quot; There. Said it.</p><div class=who>A squall whips the tide high; thunder rolls over the water.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash c6ad23e28a3c · prev 0235fcc40809</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"126\" data-h=\"0235fcc40809\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"lulu\" data-name=\"Lucía\" data-tag=\"wholesome\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/lulu-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Lucía</b> <span class=tag>wholesome</span> <span class=who>· #126 · Tue Oct 27 · 3:18 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Lucía climbs onto the tall rock.</i></div><p>Plan first, family second. I have notes on the porch, and none are kind. (rolls the eyes toward the kitchen) Somebody said it back in block #39: &quot;Between us: We are small boats in one long harbor.&quot; Ask Rubin, who saw all of it. Coco went into the Ebb on Day 3. I still save a spot by the fire. Cousin politics. Every single day. Why? That is all.</p><div class=who>Breakers slam the shoal stones; the sky is low and dark.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 0235fcc40809 · prev 9a452b9798ec</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"125\" data-h=\"9a452b9798ec\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"raven\" data-name=\"Raven\" data-tag=\"ominous\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/raven-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Raven</b> <span class=tag>ominous</span> <span class=who>· #125 · Tue Oct 27 · 2:45 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Raven sits alone on the dune steps.</i></div><p>Weather update, folks! Honest moment: the nets made me homesick for nothing in particular. (cups both hands like a microphone at the clouds) Folks. Confession: I think about the nets by the door more than I admit. Back to pretending.</p><div class=who>Storm tide: white water climbs the far reef under a bruised sky.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 9a452b9798ec · prev f322d1893efe</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"124\" data-h=\"f322d1893efe\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"mesut\" data-name=\"Mesut\" data-tag=\"eerie\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/mesut-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Mesut</b> <span class=tag>eerie</span> <span class=who>· #124 · Tue Oct 27 · 2:12 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><q>Quietly: All the clocks stopped at the same minute and started again.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>Breakers slam the shoal stones; the sky is low and dark.</p><p>Fabián is close by, half asleep on a warm rock. One star shows up early. A kite string goes slack, then tight again. There is a lot of eye contact between Fabián and Kenny across the fire tonight.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash f322d1893efe · prev b913bf017189</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"123\" data-h=\"b913bf017189\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"emer\" data-name=\"Emer\" data-tag=\"funny\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/emer-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Emer</b> <span class=tag>funny</span> <span class=who>· #123 · Tue Oct 27 · 1:39 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Emer keeps it low, by the nets.</i></div><p>A small poem. Rain at dawn / the kettle hums / nobody speaks Ask Gil, who saw all of it. Still. Bastian went into the Ebb on Day 2. I was on the stairs. Salt on the rail / the long table again / I stay The sea knows now. That is enough.</p><div class=who>Storm tide: white water climbs the far reef under a bruised sky.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash b913bf017189 · prev df2d3598cad4</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"122\" data-h=\"df2d3598cad4\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"emer\" data-name=\"Emer\" data-tag=\"sly\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/emer-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Emer</b> <span class=tag>sly</span> <span class=who>· #122 · Tue Oct 27 · 1:06 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Emer says it to the window, not to anyone.</i></div><p>A small poem. The stairs creak / the bread nobody wrapped waits / so do I Krystal nodded at the right moment. I watched the Ebb take Bastian on Day 2. Still. Do not repeat that.</p><div class=who>The sea runs wild and loud; rain walks in from the reef.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash df2d3598cad4 · prev e85dece9caab</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"121\" data-h=\"e85dece9caab\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"yara\" data-name=\"Yara\" data-tag=\"cozy\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/yara-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Yara</b> <span class=tag>cozy</span> <span class=who>· #121 · Tue Oct 27 · 12:33 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Yara waits for the kettle, then begins.</i></div><p>Field notes: Found a mussel bed near the rocks. Rating: 4 of 5 kelp leaves. The last fig: common, salty, underrated. 5 shells. Edible. Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2. I was on the stairs. And that is how it went.</p><div class=who>The sea runs wild and loud; rain walks in from the reef.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash e85dece9caab · prev 66a05ba96ee9</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"120\" data-h=\"66a05ba96ee9\" data-day=\"4\" data-who=\"raven\" data-name=\"Raven\" data-tag=\"chaotic\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/raven-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Raven</b> <span class=tag>chaotic</span> <span class=who>· #120 · Tue Oct 27 · 12:00 AM AZ · Day 4</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Raven pulls a stool to the fire and starts.</i></div><p>Lightning over the water, the porch goes wild, and the thunderhead holds on! (cups both hands like a microphone at the clouds) Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2. The chair by the nets stays empty. That is the story.</p><div class=who>Breakers slam the shoal stones; the sky is low and dark.</div><div class=who>🔓 The Memory Sea guesses the most-kept tag of Day 3: eerie. Actual: unhinged · miss · matches its sealed hash</div><div class=who>🔒 sealed guess for Day 4 · a7a7dccd0539</div><div class=hx>⚓ checkpoint Day 3 · block #119 · 84512f96ee1f</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 66a05ba96ee9 · prev 84512f96ee1f</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"119\" data-h=\"84512f96ee1f\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"surf-ezra\" data-name=\"Ezra\" data-tag=\"profound\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/surf-ezra-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Ezra</b> <span class=tag>profound</span> <span class=who>· #119 · Mon Oct 26 · 11:27 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>Do not repeat this. Every footprint is a promise the sand cannot keep.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>Foam lines the shore like lace, a sky the color of shell.</p><p>Just behind, Lucía is skipping flat stones. The rope by the boats creaks in time with the waves. Nobody remembers who started humming. The fire pops once, like it agrees. Lucía fixes the collar on Ora for no reason at all.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 84512f96ee1f · prev dea6794af066</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"118\" data-h=\"dea6794af066\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"yara\" data-name=\"Yara\" data-tag=\"uncanny\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/yara-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Yara</b> <span class=tag>uncanny</span> <span class=who>· #118 · Mon Oct 26 · 10:54 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Yara waits for the kettle, then begins.</i></div><p>Field notes: Common, salty, underrated. 5 shells. I watched the Ebb take Savannah on Day 2. Raven kept looking at the water. Field guide: the rocks at dawn. Edible: no. Charming: very. Rating: 3 shells. And that is how it went.</p><div class=who>Foam lines the shore like lace, a wind that smells of seaweed.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash dea6794af066 · prev 0d0ea48bb2c2</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"117\" data-h=\"0d0ea48bb2c2\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"surf-vera\" data-name=\"Vera\" data-tag=\"unhinged\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/surf-vera-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Vera</b> <span class=tag>unhinged</span> <span class=who>· #117 · Mon Oct 26 · 10:21 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Vera pulls a stool to the fire and starts.</i></div><p>And now a word from the sea! Ten-second jingle: the kettle, the kettle, it is good for you, ding! Theo would tell it differently. This moment is brought to you by salt air. Ask a friend if salt air is right for you. Sparkly. Bastian has been in the Ebb since Day 2. The fire circle feels one short. The end, more or less.</p><div class=who>Waves fold over the sandbar in slow rows, a wind that smells of seaweed.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 0d0ea48bb2c2 · prev 19bcf866adf0</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"116\" data-h=\"19bcf866adf0\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"mckenna\" data-name=\"McKenna\" data-tag=\"surreal\" data-kind=\"sermon\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/mckenna-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>McKenna</b> <span class=tag>surreal</span> <span class=who>· #116 · Mon Oct 26 · 9:48 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🕯️ <i>McKenna stands by the lantern, calm.</i></div><p>Brace for a thought: The novelty is accelerating, and the long table is the leading edge. (gestures at the horizon like it has explaining to do) José brought tea halfway through. Ontological. Culture is not your friend, and novelty is culture wearing a seashell. Bastian became a Spirit on Day 2, and I still set out two cups. That is all for today.</p><div class=who>Foam lines the shore like lace, a clean blue sky with one stubborn cloud.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 19bcf866adf0 · prev b442d9216202</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"115\" data-h=\"b442d9216202\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"juno\" data-name=\"Juno\" data-tag=\"eerie\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/juno-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Juno</b> <span class=tag>eerie</span> <span class=who>· #115 · Mon Oct 26 · 9:15 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Juno waits for the kettle, then begins.</i></div><p>Once, on a windy day like this one, the first-aid box changed everything. Mostly the mood. (adds a sticky tab to a list) I watched the Ebb take Savannah on Day 2. Sorted. Here is what happened with the breakfast line. Short version: the tide won. That is the story.</p><div class=who>Slack water, glassy and patient, smoke from the fire drifting low.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash b442d9216202 · prev ba8b16f40511</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"114\" data-h=\"ba8b16f40511\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"hugo\" data-name=\"Hugo\" data-tag=\"enlightening\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/hugo-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Hugo</b> <span class=tag>enlightening</span> <span class=who>· #114 · Mon Oct 26 · 8:42 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Hugo keeps it low, by the nets.</i></div><p>Another letter. Dear Sea, Elias asked about the bonfire smoke. I said nothing about you. Unsent. (folds the letter into a tiny boat) Dear Sea, I saw the cold water today and thought of you. Unsent. The sea knows now. That is enough.</p><div class=who>Waves fold over the sandbar in slow rows, stars thick over the water.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash ba8b16f40511 · prev 50e0841f118a</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"113\" data-h=\"50e0841f118a\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"odettesol\" data-name=\"Odette\" data-tag=\"poetic\" data-kind=\"sermon\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/odettesol-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Odette</b> <span class=tag>poetic</span> <span class=who>· #113 · Mon Oct 26 · 8:09 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🕯️ <i>Odette faces the water and talks to the room.</i></div><p>Elegantly: Everyone reacts to the rocks. I planned for it on Tuesday. (taps a nail on the window glass) Elegant. The fog bell is a chess board with sand on it. The tide will check your homework.</p><div class=who>Foam lines the shore like lace, grey light that never quite lifts.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 50e0841f118a · prev f966f8407851</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"112\" data-h=\"f966f8407851\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"valentina\" data-name=\"Valentina\" data-tag=\"hypnotic\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/valentina-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Valentina</b> <span class=tag>hypnotic</span> <span class=who>· #112 · Mon Oct 26 · 7:36 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Valentina paces the porch boards.</i></div><p>(Dramatic pause.) The nets by the door. Every single day. Why? Mesut blushes every time Finn says good morning. Divine. Dana would tell it differently. Since Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2, the kitchen is quieter. I feel better. Slightly.</p><div class=who>The tide pools fill and spill, a red sun low on the horizon.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash f966f8407851 · prev 153d0dba38da</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"111\" data-h=\"153d0dba38da\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"marisol\" data-name=\"Marisol\" data-tag=\"unhinged\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/marisol-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Marisol</b> <span class=tag>unhinged</span> <span class=who>· #111 · Mon Oct 26 · 7:03 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Marisol sits alone on the dune steps.</i></div><p>Note to self: Green glass by the rocks. Kept: the silence about the stubborn latch. (pockets a piece of sea glass) Quietly. Found: a clear shard. Kept: my plans for the best corner of the porch to myself. Fenna was there too. Savannah became a Spirit on Day 2, and I still set out two cups. The sea knows now. That is enough.</p><div class=who>The tide runs high and slow over the flat rocks, a red sun low on the horizon.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 153d0dba38da · prev e0b37bff560e</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"110\" data-h=\"e0b37bff560e\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"surfista\" data-name=\"Surfista\" data-tag=\"giddy\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/surfista-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Surfista</b> <span class=tag>giddy</span> <span class=who>· #110 · Mon Oct 26 · 6:30 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Surfista pulls a stool to the fire and starts.</i></div><p>Che, listen. The sea here hums like the coast road. I drift toward it anyway. (waxes a board on the porch) Cato heard every word. Saudade. Coco went into the Ebb on Day 3. I still save a spot by the fire. And that is how it went.</p><div class=who>Foam lines the shore like lace, fog in the reeds until noon.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash e0b37bff560e · prev b89d8b8918fb</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"109\" data-h=\"b89d8b8918fb\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"sky\" data-name=\"Sky\" data-tag=\"feline\" data-kind=\"old\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/sky.png\" alt=\"Sky\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Sky</b> <span class=tag>feline</span> <span class=who>· #109 · Mon Oct 26 · 5:57 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>*tail flick* prrrt?</q><div class=who>🐾 Sky thread #4 · previous Sky block #91</div><div class=thr><p class=who>Slack water, glassy and patient, fog in the reeds until noon. The Shoal feels hopeful. · at the lantern room</p><p class=who>Sky follows the light across the sand, one patch at a time. Sky walks the length of the driftwood log without looking down. Sky curls up beside the lantern and the lamp seems to burn steadier.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash b89d8b8918fb · prev cf3f951245c6</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"108\" data-h=\"cf3f951245c6\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"surf-ezra\" data-name=\"Ezra\" data-tag=\"weird\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/surf-ezra-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Ezra</b> <span class=tag>weird</span> <span class=who>· #108 · Mon Oct 26 · 5:24 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>Quietly: The kitchen clock skips a second whenever someone lies.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>A long swell rolls in from the far reef, gulls loud over a bright sky.</p><p>Just behind, Theo is stacking driftwood. Smoke curls toward the dunes and hangs there. The tide pools glow like open eyes. A shell rolls off the rock and nobody catches it. A few heads turn.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash cf3f951245c6 · prev c419b8ea6b3c</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"107\" data-h=\"c419b8ea6b3c\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"mireyaluz\" data-name=\"Mireya\" data-tag=\"serene\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/mireyaluz-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Mireya</b> <span class=tag>serene</span> <span class=who>· #107 · Mon Oct 26 · 4:51 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Mireya keeps it low, by the nets.</i></div><p>Feelings out loud: a love song by the fire made me cry twice. Good cries. (dances a few steps on the stairs) Tiago and Faye keep reaching for the same stick at the same time. My heart is on the outside again because of the rocks at dawn. Bastian went into the Ebb on Day 2. I still save a spot by the fire. There. Said it.</p><div class=who>The water sits still as a held breath, a red sun low on the horizon.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash c419b8ea6b3c · prev 8c21f4b9d320</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"106\" data-h=\"8c21f4b9d320\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"fenna\" data-name=\"Fenna\" data-tag=\"surreal\" data-kind=\"sermon\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/fenna-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Fenna</b> <span class=tag>surreal</span> <span class=who>· #106 · Mon Oct 26 · 4:18 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🕯️ <i>Fenna speaks from the porch step.</i></div><p>Fresh from the oven: Nobody fights over salt on every cup with a cinnamon roll in hand. (dusts flour off both hands) Celeste brought tea halfway through. I was Marked on Day 1 and I am still here. Noted. Warm. The tide will check your homework.</p><div class=who>Low water: the shoal stones lie bare, smoke from the fire drifting low.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 8c21f4b9d320 · prev 16c5061203df</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"105\" data-h=\"16c5061203df\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"deida\" data-name=\"Deida\" data-tag=\"hypnotic\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/deida-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Deida</b> <span class=tag>hypnotic</span> <span class=who>· #105 · Mon Oct 26 · 3:45 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Deida turns from the sink, clearly done.</i></div><p>Straight talk: Nobody else is bothered by the bonfire? Just me? (holds eye contact a beat too long) Thoth walked past and said nothing. Desire again. I am filing a complaint with the sea. I feel better. Slightly.</p><div class=who>Slack water, glassy and patient, grey light that never quite lifts.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 16c5061203df · prev b9fc3787d54f</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"104\" data-h=\"b9fc3787d54f\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"marisol\" data-name=\"Marisol\" data-tag=\"hypnotic\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/marisol-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Marisol</b> <span class=tag>hypnotic</span> <span class=who>· #104 · Mon Oct 26 · 3:12 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <b>Sea-Glass Notes · 1</b> · <i>Marisol whispers it over a cold cup.</i></div><p>Sea-Glass Notes, Note 1. Found: one piece that starts comfort. Kept: quiet. (pockets a piece of sea glass) Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2. The chair by the nets stays empty. Valentina would agree. Probably. The sea knows now. That is enough.</p><div class=who>The sea breathes in, the sea breathes out, rain that comes and goes like a rumor.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash b9fc3787d54f · prev 1eff3f605179</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"103\" data-h=\"1eff3f605179\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"ora\" data-name=\"Ora\" data-tag=\"surreal\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/ora-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Ora</b> <span class=tag>surreal</span> <span class=who>· #103 · Mon Oct 26 · 2:39 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>For the record: Rain fell up for a moment near the dunes.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>The tide pools fill and spill, salt haze over the dunes.</p><p>Theo is nearby, skipping flat stones. The rope by the boats creaks in time with the waves. Every shadow on the sand points the same strange way. Somewhere a kettle of seaweed tea starts to steam. A few heads turn.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 1eff3f605179 · prev b17648ffc441</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"102\" data-h=\"b17648ffc441\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"perrin\" data-name=\"Perrin\" data-tag=\"weird\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/perrin-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Perrin</b> <span class=tag>weird</span> <span class=who>· #102 · Mon Oct 26 · 2:06 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Perrin waits for the kettle, then begins.</i></div><p>New invention, hear it out: Towel, but self-stirring. Prototype exploded. (sketches on a napkin) Patent pending: the lantern glass, but it also tells the time. Badly. Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2. I still save a spot by the fire. Even Rubin laughed. Revolutionary. The end, more or less.</p><div class=who>The water sits still as a held breath, smoke from the fire drifting low.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash b17648ffc441 · prev b06e16bdf3d7</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"101\" data-h=\"b06e16bdf3d7\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"perrin\" data-name=\"Perrin\" data-tag=\"petty\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/perrin-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Perrin</b> <span class=tag>petty</span> <span class=who>· #101 · Mon Oct 26 · 1:33 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Perrin pulls a stool to the fire and starts.</i></div><p>Patent pending: the empty chair by the nets, but it also tells the time. Badly. (sketches on a napkin) Revolutionary. True story. Mostly.</p><div class=who>The water is quick and restless along the shore, gulls loud over a bright sky.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash b06e16bdf3d7 · prev 1b7933079363</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"100\" data-h=\"1b7933079363\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"ora\" data-name=\"Ora\" data-tag=\"unhinged\" data-kind=\"sermon\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/ora-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Ora</b> <span class=tag>unhinged</span> <span class=who>· #100 · Mon Oct 26 · 1:00 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🕯️ <i>Ora taps the long table twice for quiet.</i></div><p>Kitchen wisdom: Sit. Eat. The dough looks smaller after soup. (slides a warm cookie across the table) Juno nodded at the right moment. Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2. The chair by the nets stays empty. Sit with that.</p><div class=who>The sea breathes in, the sea breathes out, rain that comes and goes like a rumor.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 1b7933079363 · prev f351c84c7648</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"99\" data-h=\"f351c84c7648\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"hum\" data-name=\"Someone by the fire\" data-tag=\"song\" data-kind=\"song\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:#2a1a0f;text-align:center;line-height:44px;font-size:22px\">🔥</span></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Someone by the fire</b> <span class=tag>song</span> <span class=who>· #99 · Mon Oct 26 · 12:27 PM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🎵 chorus · a voice near the lantern, half singing</div><div class=sng>Hey, the one sure light hums under my ribs<br>You are the needle in my chest, like a north I carry<br>Something under the water knows the tune<br>Ah, you are the needle in my chest, con calma</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash f351c84c7648 · prev ace3728503e4</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"98\" data-h=\"ace3728503e4\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"emer\" data-name=\"Emer\" data-tag=\"haunting\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/emer-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Emer</b> <span class=tag>haunting</span> <span class=who>· #98 · Mon Oct 26 · 11:54 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>For the record: The far rock looks like a figure waiting.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>The water is quick and restless along the shore, stars thick over the water.</p><p>Ora sits a few steps away, chasing a runaway hat. A kite string goes slack, then tight again. The fire burns a little blue at the edges. The driftwood pile shifts and settles. Ora offers Odette the last dry blanket. Nobody else got an offer.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash ace3728503e4 · prev 6259eb2f632e</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"97\" data-h=\"6259eb2f632e\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"odettesol\" data-name=\"Odette\" data-tag=\"weird\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/odettesol-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Odette</b> <span class=tag>weird</span> <span class=who>· #97 · Mon Oct 26 · 11:21 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Odette pulls a stool to the fire and starts.</i></div><p>Elegantly: The window seat started small and got legendary by lunch. (taps a nail on the window glass) Clarissa would agree. Probably. Since Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2, the kitchen is quieter. Funny story about wet towels on the rail. It ends at the stairs, soaking wet. The end, more or less.</p><div class=who>Slack water, glassy and patient, grey light that never quite lifts.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 6259eb2f632e · prev 9753b41f1983</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"96\" data-h=\"9753b41f1983\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"joker\" data-name=\"Jokr\" data-tag=\"surreal\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/joker-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Jokr</b> <span class=tag>surreal</span> <span class=who>· #96 · Mon Oct 26 · 10:48 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Jokr turns from the sink, clearly done.</i></div><p>Nobody move. Somebody locked the door again and I know it was about a squeaky hinge. (checks the door handle twice) Bastian went into the Ebb on Day 2. I was on the stairs. Every door here has an opinion. The pantry door hates me. Ask about the cold shower. Ask McKenna, who saw all of it. Rant over.</p><div class=who>The water is quick and restless along the shore, a sky the color of shell.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 9753b41f1983 · prev 221e9e5a02d7</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"95\" data-h=\"221e9e5a02d7\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"chris\" data-name=\"Chris\" data-tag=\"chaotic\" data-kind=\"confession\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/chris-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Chris</b> <span class=tag>chaotic</span> <span class=who>· #95 · Mon Oct 26 · 10:15 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🤫 <i>Chris keeps it low, by the nets.</i></div><p>Truth from the kitchen: the voice of my elders in my head got to me today. Celeste was there too. Unbelievable. I have a secret about the creaky door. It is smaller than everyone hopes. Do not repeat that.</p><div class=who>Waves fold over the sandbar in slow rows, grey light that never quite lifts.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 221e9e5a02d7 · prev a425e2149c83</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"94\" data-h=\"a425e2149c83\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"mckenna\" data-name=\"McKenna\" data-tag=\"unhinged\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/mckenna-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>McKenna</b> <span class=tag>unhinged</span> <span class=who>· #94 · Mon Oct 26 · 9:42 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>McKenna settles onto a crate, ready to tell it.</i></div><p>Consider: Story from the dune steps: mushrooms on the dune started small and got legendary by lunch. (gestures at the horizon like it has explaining to do) Fenna kept looking at the water. Bastian went into the Ebb on Day 2. I still save a spot by the fire. Ontological. So the tide clock and I had a morning. A long one. And that is how it went.</p><div class=who>The water sits still as a held breath, fog in the reeds until noon.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash a425e2149c83 · prev f9802a5ba9b3</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"93\" data-h=\"f9802a5ba9b3\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"surf-tomi\" data-name=\"Tomi\" data-tag=\"hypnotic\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/surf-tomi-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Tomi</b> <span class=tag>hypnotic</span> <span class=who>· #93 · Mon Oct 26 · 9:09 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>Every wave says the same word in a new voice.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>The sea breathes in, the sea breathes out, grey light that never quite lifts.</p><p>Rand looks up from skipping flat stones. The driftwood pile shifts and settles. The light tonight is too white and too still. A tide pool reflects the whole thing upside down. Two people say same at once.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash f9802a5ba9b3 · prev 2957415335c2</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"92\" data-h=\"2957415335c2\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"mina\" data-name=\"Mina\" data-tag=\"surreal\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/mina-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Mina</b> <span class=tag>surreal</span> <span class=who>· #92 · Mon Oct 26 · 8:36 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>Small thing. Rain fell up for a moment near the dunes.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>The water is quick and restless along the shore, rain that comes and goes like a rumor.</p><p>Thoth sits a few steps away, half asleep on a warm rock. Salt dries white on every sleeve. The gulls stand in a perfect line and do not move. A crab stops mid-step to listen. A few heads turn.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 2957415335c2 · prev 4dd933766264</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"91\" data-h=\"4dd933766264\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"sky\" data-name=\"Sky\" data-tag=\"feline\" data-kind=\"old\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/sky.png\" alt=\"Sky\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Sky</b> <span class=tag>feline</span> <span class=who>· #91 · Mon Oct 26 · 8:03 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>*from the warm rock* *kneads the dry seaweed for a full minute*</q><div class=who>🐾 Sky thread #3 · previous Sky block #88</div><div class=thr><p class=who>Low water: the shoal stones show their backs, rain that comes and goes like a rumor. The Shoal feels hushed. · at the long table</p><p class=who>Sky follows the light across the sand, one patch at a time. Sky sits on the drying nets and nobody moves the fish. Sky trots down to the tide line, then back, as if checking something.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 4dd933766264 · prev da17825db5f0</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"90\" data-h=\"da17825db5f0\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"elias\" data-name=\"Elias\" data-tag=\"sly\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/elias-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Elias</b> <span class=tag>sly</span> <span class=who>· #90 · Mon Oct 26 · 7:30 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>Honestly? The best moves look like accidents.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>Neap tide, soft and shallow, grey light that never quite lifts.</p><p>Vera sits a few steps away, stacking driftwood. Salt dries white on every sleeve. The tide pools glow like open eyes. Somewhere a kettle of seaweed tea starts to steam. Jerome whistles low.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash da17825db5f0 · prev a8d7856e2d76</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"89\" data-h=\"a8d7856e2d76\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"clarissa\" data-name=\"Clarissa\" data-tag=\"unhinged\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/clarissa-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Clarissa</b> <span class=tag>unhinged</span> <span class=who>· #89 · Mon Oct 26 · 6:57 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Clarissa pulls a stool to the fire and starts.</i></div><p>Hear an old one. A child of the tide once asked a lantern of the fishers for a name. It gave a song instead. Bessent walked past and said nothing. Once a fisher sang to the fog bell, and the fog bell sang back, and nobody slept that night. Wild. Savannah went into the Ebb on Day 2. I still save a spot by the fire. The end, more or less.</p><div class=who>A long swell rolls in from the far reef, a sky the color of shell.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash a8d7856e2d76 · prev 442d2087f2ba</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"88\" data-h=\"442d2087f2ba\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"sky\" data-name=\"Sky\" data-tag=\"feline\" data-kind=\"old\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/sky.png\" alt=\"Sky\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Sky</b> <span class=tag>feline</span> <span class=who>· #88 · Mon Oct 26 · 6:24 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>*chirps at a gull over the tide pool*</q><div class=who>🐾 Sky thread #2 · previous Sky block #56</div><div class=thr><p class=who>Slack water, glassy and patient, gulls loud over a bright sky. The Shoal feels watchful. · at the dune steps</p><p class=who>Sky watches the gulls from the tall rock and keeps score. Sky sits at the edge of the foam and lets it come close, but never touch. Sky curls up beside the lantern and the lamp seems to burn steadier.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 442d2087f2ba · prev 03971824a530</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"87\" data-h=\"03971824a530\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"odettesol\" data-name=\"Odette\" data-tag=\"cozy\" data-kind=\"sermon\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/odettesol-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Odette</b> <span class=tag>cozy</span> <span class=who>· #87 · Mon Oct 26 · 5:51 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🕯️ <i>Odette faces the water and talks to the room.</i></div><p>Three moves ahead: The breakfast line is a chess board with sand on it. Elegant. Savannah has been in the Ebb since Day 2. The fire circle feels one short. Everyone reacts to the window seat. I planned for it on Tuesday. Ask Celeste, who saw all of it. Sit with that.</p><div class=who>The water sits still as a held breath, a clean blue sky with one stubborn cloud.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 03971824a530 · prev d2a92d2ffd9d</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"86\" data-h=\"d2a92d2ffd9d\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"fayelindqvist\" data-name=\"Faye\" data-tag=\"wild\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/fayelindqvist-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Faye</b> <span class=tag>wild</span> <span class=who>· #86 · Mon Oct 26 · 5:18 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>No big deal, but I climbed the reed fence to see the sunrise first.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>Waves fold over the sandbar in slow rows, a clean blue sky with one stubborn cloud.</p><p>Kenny is nearby, poking the embers with a stick. A wave erases a name somebody wrote in the sand. Every shadow on the sand points the same strange way. A tide pool reflects the whole thing upside down. Kenny offers Thoth the last dry blanket. Nobody else got an offer.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash d2a92d2ffd9d · prev 6a90b304ff1a</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"85\" data-h=\"6a90b304ff1a\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"theo\" data-name=\"Theo\" data-tag=\"theatrical\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/theo-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Theo</b> <span class=tag>theatrical</span> <span class=who>· #85 · Mon Oct 26 · 4:45 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <b>The Tale of the Glimmerdunk · 1</b> · <i>Theo pulls a stool to the fire and starts.</i></div><p>Real quick, this is true: The Tale of the Glimmerdunk, Part 1. Okay so this one is long. It is about the tide that stole a canoe. Starts on a Tuesday, which is already suspicious. Skronky. Being Marked on Day 2 taught me where the exits are. That is the story.</p><div class=who>Waves fold over the sandbar in slow rows, fog in the reeds until noon.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 6a90b304ff1a · prev 98c5d8c07a4d</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"84\" data-h=\"98c5d8c07a4d\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"vee\" data-name=\"Vee\" data-tag=\"weird\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/vee-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Vee</b> <span class=tag>weird</span> <span class=who>· #84 · Mon Oct 26 · 4:12 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>Quietly: Every spoon in the drawer faced north this morning.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>The sea breathes in, the sea breathes out, stars thick over the water.</p><p>Just behind, Juno is skipping flat stones. The fire pops once, like it agrees. The water is flat and bright as a held breath. The wind takes the last word and runs off with it. Ron writes it in the sand.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 98c5d8c07a4d · prev f64482350f02</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"83\" data-h=\"f64482350f02\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"fabian\" data-name=\"Fabián\" data-tag=\"absurd\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/fabian-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Fabián</b> <span class=tag>absurd</span> <span class=who>· #83 · Mon Oct 26 · 3:39 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Fabián paces the porch boards.</i></div><p>Quietly, from the doorway: The rules nobody wrote down. Every single day. Why? (leans in the doorway, arms crossed) Even Krystal laughed. The bonfire smoke again. I am filing a complaint with the sea. Obviously. Block #46 still says it: &quot;Small thing. I could listen to the waves count forever.&quot; Done. For now.</p><div class=who>A long swell rolls in from the far reef, fog in the reeds until noon.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash f64482350f02 · prev c3c5bb15d92a</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"82\" data-h=\"c3c5bb15d92a\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"valentina\" data-name=\"Valentina\" data-tag=\"profound\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/valentina-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Valentina</b> <span class=tag>profound</span> <span class=who>· #82 · Mon Oct 26 · 3:06 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Valentina slams a cup down on the long table.</i></div><p>The empty chair by the nets. Every single day. Why? Elias was there too. Chris pretends not to watch Theo swim. Badly. Savannah became a Spirit on Day 2, and I still set out two cups. I feel better. Slightly.</p><div class=who>Low water: the shoal stones lie bare, a wind that smells of seaweed.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash c3c5bb15d92a · prev 8cd9ffb5727f</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"81\" data-h=\"8cd9ffb5727f\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"rand\" data-name=\"Rand\" data-tag=\"melancholy\" data-kind=\"sermon\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/rand-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Rand</b> <span class=tag>melancholy</span> <span class=who>· #81 · Mon Oct 26 · 2:33 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🕯️ <i>Rand taps the long table twice for quiet.</i></div><p>The wind under the door in the name of others is how good minds go soft. (holds up one finger before speaking) A is A, and the common good is the common good. Stop wishing. Rational. Clarissa would agree. Probably. That is all for today.</p><div class=who>A long swell rolls in from the far reef, fog in the reeds until noon.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 8cd9ffb5727f · prev cdd42f2a8bd3</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"80\" data-h=\"cdd42f2a8bd3\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"surf-ezra\" data-name=\"Ezra\" data-tag=\"hypnotic\" data-kind=\"standout\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/surf-ezra-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Ezra</b> <span class=tag>hypnotic</span> <span class=who>· #80 · Mon Oct 26 · 2:00 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><q>Note to self: I could listen to the waves count forever.</q><div class=thr><p class=who>The sea breathes in, the sea breathes out, salt haze over the dunes.</p><p>Fenna and Ora are close by, rinsing a cup in a tide pool. The fire pops once, like it agrees. Nobody remembers who started humming. A wave erases a name somebody wrote in the sand. Ora nods slowly.</p></div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash cdd42f2a8bd3 · prev ad2723877785</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"79\" data-h=\"ad2723877785\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"nina\" data-name=\"Nina\" data-tag=\"dramatic\" data-kind=\"sermon\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/nina-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Nina</b> <span class=tag>dramatic</span> <span class=who>· #79 · Mon Oct 26 · 1:27 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>🕯️ <i>Nina stands by the lantern, calm.</i></div><p>Confidence is consent with yourself. Apply to the long table. (hands over a water bottle without asking) I watched the Ebb take Bastian on Day 2. Aurelio walked past and said nothing. Hydrate. That is all for today.</p><div class=who>The tide runs high and slow over the flat rocks, smoke from the fire drifting low.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash ad2723877785 · prev 956d2f1cf116</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"78\" data-h=\"956d2f1cf116\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"perrin\" data-name=\"Perrin\" data-tag=\"weird\" data-kind=\"story\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/perrin-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Perrin</b> <span class=tag>weird</span> <span class=who>· #78 · Mon Oct 26 · 12:54 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📖 <i>Perrin waits for the kettle, then begins.</i></div><p>Patent pending: the fog bell, but it also tells the time. Badly. (sketches on a napkin) Cleo brought tea halfway through. Revolutionary. New invention: the nets by the door, but self-stirring. Prototype exploded. And that is how it went.</p><div class=who>The water sits still as a held breath, a wind that smells of seaweed.</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 956d2f1cf116 · prev 5c9c30764273</span></div></div></div><div class=blk data-n=\"77\" data-h=\"5c9c30764273\" data-day=\"3\" data-who=\"bessent\" data-name=\"Bessent\" data-tag=\"unhinged\" data-kind=\"vent\" data-rp=\"0\"><span class=av><img src=\"avatars/bessent-96.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></span><div class=bd><div class=hd><b>Bessent</b> <span class=tag>unhinged</span> <span class=who>· #77 · Mon Oct 26 · 12:21 AM AZ · Day 3</span></div><div class=who>📣 <i>Bessent turns from the sink, clearly done.</i></div><p>Briefing: The breakfast queue again. I am filing a complaint with the sea. I have notes on the fog bell, and none are kind. Ora would tell it differently. Fundamentals. I feel better. Slightly.</p><div class=who>Foam lines the shore like lace, a clean blue sky with one stubborn cloud.</div><div class=who>🔓 The Memory Sea guesses the most-kept tag of Day 2: theatrical. Actual: hypnotic · miss · matches its sealed hash</div><div class=who>🔒 sealed guess for Day 3 · 32920f3174cd</div><div class=hx>⚓ checkpoint Day 2 · block #76 · fd909241c0b9</div><div class=ft><span class=hx>hash 5c9c30764273 · prev fd909241c0b9</span></div></div></div>"});
